1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,361
This is Talang,
a sealed-bid repo desk on Canton.

2
00:00:04,911 --> 00:00:08,726
Repo is how bond holders
raise cash without selling.

3
00:00:08,726 --> 00:00:13,197
But asking five lenders for a price
tells all five you need money.

4
00:00:13,747 --> 00:00:17,366
On Talang, a quote goes
to the borrower alone.

5
00:00:17,366 --> 00:00:20,218
Canton never sends it to a rival's node.

6
00:00:20,768 --> 00:00:25,676
Here's the desk, typed in live.
The borrower asks three lenders

7
00:00:25,676 --> 00:00:30,489
for five point three million USDC
against sixty Treasury notes.

8
00:00:31,039 --> 00:00:34,184
Lender A types its rate and haircut,

9
00:00:34,184 --> 00:00:37,224
and seals the quote,
with the cash locked behind it.

10
00:00:37,224 --> 00:00:39,774
Its node shows only its own quotes.

11
00:00:40,324 --> 00:00:44,626
Lender B quotes the lowest rate,
with a six percent haircut.

12
00:00:44,626 --> 00:00:48,505
Lender C quotes four
ninety-five, with three.

13
00:00:51,204 --> 00:00:56,138
The borrower sees three sealed quotes.
B's is short at the mark,

14
00:00:56,138 --> 00:00:58,585
so it takes the cheapest one that covers.

15
00:00:58,585 --> 00:01:02,254
Cash and collateral
move in one transaction.

16
00:01:02,804 --> 00:01:06,133
Lender B learns its rank, nothing else.

17
00:01:06,133 --> 00:01:10,485
Since version 1.2.0, it isn't
even an informee of the award.

18
00:01:11,035 --> 00:01:14,180
The regulator sees best execution:

19
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:17,809
the winner ranked second on rate,
and no lender is named.

20
00:01:18,359 --> 00:01:21,991
Then the valuation agent
publishes a lower mark.

21
00:01:21,991 --> 00:01:25,725
Lender A's repo is now short,
so it calls margin.

22
00:01:29,799 --> 00:01:34,536
But one agent shouldn't set
the mark alone. So a committee does:

23
00:01:34,536 --> 00:01:39,523
one decentralized party on three nodes,
run through BitSafe's DecMan.

24
00:01:39,523 --> 00:01:41,533
Two of three must confirm.

25
00:01:42,083 --> 00:01:46,057
Node one proposes a markdown and confirms,

26
00:01:46,057 --> 00:01:50,975
which alone publishes nothing.
Node two confirms in its own DecMan.

27
00:01:52,975 --> 00:01:56,620
Execute, and the mark
is published as the committee.

28
00:01:56,620 --> 00:02:01,236
Node three didn't vote,
but its audit trail shows every step.

29
00:02:03,663 --> 00:02:08,384
The lender calls margin with that mark.
No single pricer could have moved it.

30
00:02:08,934 --> 00:02:13,882
With one node stopped, the committee
still published; with two, it couldn't.

31
00:02:13,882 --> 00:02:18,168
And the same flow ran
on the NODERS DevNet participant.

32
00:02:18,718 --> 00:02:22,876
Version 1.2.0 of the contract
is now vetted there too.

33
00:02:22,876 --> 00:02:27,968
It adds a minimum transfer on margin
calls, lender-signed haircut schedules,

34
00:02:27,968 --> 00:02:32,742
and a master agreement with close-out
netting, all driven from the desk.

35
00:02:33,292 --> 00:02:39,647
Both legs can be real tokens. On DevNet,
a repo ran with Canton Coin cash and

36
00:02:39,647 --> 00:02:45,224
CBTC collateral, each allocated through
its registry and settled at repurchase.

37
00:02:45,774 --> 00:02:52,642
When a call on a stress mark went
unanswered, the default ran too:

38
00:02:52,642 --> 00:02:57,547
0.001 CBTC to lender A,
through the DA Utility registry.

39
00:02:58,097 --> 00:03:02,518
The desk also connects to a real
Grofty wallet on Canton TestNet.

40
00:03:02,518 --> 00:03:06,755
Each desk command is signed in Grofty
and checked before it's submitted,

41
00:03:06,755 --> 00:03:11,374
and a one Canton Coin venue fee
is paid from the wallet on TestNet.

42
00:03:11,374 --> 00:03:16,674
The signed Talang commands ran
on a local sandbox, not yet on TestNet.

43
00:03:17,224 --> 00:03:22,421
Each desk can have an AI agent over MCP.
It reads only its own node,

44
00:03:22,421 --> 00:03:26,616
so a lender's agent never
sees a rival's rate.

45
00:03:27,166 --> 00:03:32,732
The business is a venue fee, collected
inside every repurchase and roll,

46
00:03:32,732 --> 00:03:36,466
so it can't be skipped.
It's built, with no revenue yet.

47
00:03:37,016 --> 00:03:42,595
Next: a two-week shadow book on DevNet,
then small live repos on MainNet.

48
00:03:42,595 --> 00:03:49,737
Not done yet: USDCx, Talang commands
on TestNet, and any pilot user.

49
00:03:50,287 --> 00:03:55,155
That's Talang. The live desk
and the code are on screen now.

